<task id="010" project="spaarkeai-compose-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Persist w14:paraId into the retained package on ingest (FR-01)</title>
    <phase>1 Backend ingest</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies BFF `.cs` (tags include bff-api), touches the ingest write path (retained package bytes), carries a seam DoD (ADR-038) — code-review + adr-check MUST run at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Bounded extension of a single existing KEEP asset (`ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper`) with a clear reference impl to reuse (`ParaIdPreParser`/`AnnotationReanchorService.ExtractParaIds`); no cross-cutting architecture change.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,docx</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
    <assigned>unassigned</assigned>
    <started></started>
    <completed></completed>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Extend `ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper` so that on ingest every editable `w:p` that lacks a
    `w14:paraId` gets one MINTED and WRITTEN INTO the retained shadow package bytes — not merely
    carried in the projection. Today the stamper mints ids for the projection/snapshot; R4 requires the
    id to be DURABLE across round-trips (load → save → reload), so it MUST be persisted into the OOXML
    of the retained package that becomes the source of truth (invariant I-1, I-3). Mint deterministically
    and write into the DOM (never string-edit `document.xml`); reuse `ParaIdPreParser` /
    `AnnotationReanchorService.ExtractParaIds` for the document-order paragraph walk (including table
    cells and nested tables) so the id set is complete. This MUST be idempotent: a paragraph that already
    carries a `w14:paraId` is left untouched (never re-minted). The Patch Engine (Phase 3) later resolves
    nodes O(1) by these ids, so a missing or duplicated id is a correctness defect, not a cosmetic one.
    Be literal: mint-if-absent, write-into-retained-bytes, leave-existing-alone.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 developer fluent in `DocumentFormat.OpenXml` DOM mutation (the `w14:paraId` attribute
    on `w:p`, the `w14` namespace, `WordprocessingDocument` open/save round-trips) and the existing
    Compose ingest pipeline (`ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper`, `ParaIdPreParser`, `AnnotationReanchorService`).
    Understands the byte[]-in/byte[]-out facade discipline (ADR-007) and that the retained package — not
    the projection — is the source of truth (I-1).
  </role>

  <goal>
    On ingest, every editable `w:p` in the retained package carries a persisted, unique `w14:paraId`
    written into the retained bytes; ids survive a load → save → reload round-trip; a document that
    already has paraIds is not re-minted (idempotent). The paragraph walk covers table cells and nested
    tables via the reused extraction helper, so no editable paragraph is missed.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5 "Ingest (backend)": "ensure every editable `w:p` has a `w14:paraId` (mint + **persist**
      if missing)". As-built inventory KEEP list: `ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper` "Mints + stamps paraIds
      onto id-less paragraphs. **Extend** to persist ids into the shadow package on ingest." Today the
      stamper produces the projection-carried id map but the id is not guaranteed durable in the retained
      bytes; R4 makes the retained package the authoritative model (I-1), so the id MUST live in those
      bytes. `ParaIdPreParser` / `AnnotationReanchorService.ExtractParaIds` already do the document-order
      walk incl. table cells — reuse them, do not re-implement. Word regenerates paraIds on external
      tracked-change saves; that cross-session case is `AnnotationReanchorService`'s job (fuzzy fallback),
      not this task's — see escalation.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper.cs — extend to mint-if-absent AND write the `w14:paraId` into the retained package DOM; keep idempotent for pre-existing ids</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ParaIdPreParser.cs — document-order paraId extraction to reuse for the paragraph walk</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs — `ExtractParaIds` document-order walk incl. table cells / nested tables (reuse; do not re-implement)</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs — consumes the stamped package; keep the projection paraId map consistent with the persisted ids</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5 (Ingest), §3 (I-1/I-3)</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-01, NFR-05</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Shadow-Document ADR — establishes the retained-package-as-source-of-truth model this task persists ids into.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-01">On load, every editable `w:p` MUST carry a persisted `w14:paraId` (minted + written into the retained package if absent). Scope: the persistence is into the RETAINED PACKAGE BYTES, not just the projection map. MUST NOT re-mint a paragraph that already has a paraId (idempotent).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / I-1,I-3">The retained OOXML package is the authoritative model; addressing is by stable `w14:paraId`. Scope: mint deterministically; write into the DOM; the id set must be unique across the whole document (incl. table cells / nested tables).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Patch/ingest stays `byte[]`-in/`byte[]`-out; no `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/`; the SPE hop stays behind `SpeFileStore`. Scope: this task operates on package bytes only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">`Services/Compose/` injects NO AI internals; Tier-1 NetArchTest stays green. Scope: no `IOpenAiClient`/executor/routing type introduced.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 Placement Justification">Extends an existing KEEP asset in `Services/Compose/` (no new service/DI). State the Placement Justification (mint/persist stays in `Services/Compose/`, reuses the stamper + extraction seams) in the PR; cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. Run `/conflict-check` before the BFF PR (`Services/Compose/` overlaps r1/r2/r3 + ai-architecture-redesign-r2).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Mutate the OpenXml DOM — never string-edit `document.xml`. Through-the-wire proof is task 013's seam slice; NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 publish-size">Report BFF publish size absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (incl. PDBs), ≤60 MB; no new runtime package expected; verify no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Persisting w14:paraId into retained OOXML on ingest; DOM mutation via DocumentFormat.OpenXml; document-order paragraph walk incl. table cells; BFF facade discipline + hygiene</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
