    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Document-order paraId extraction (reuse)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs">
        `ExtractParaIds` walks `w:p` in document order including table cells / nested tables — reuse this walk to enumerate the paragraphs that need minting rather than re-implementing the traversal.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Mint-if-absent stamper (extend)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper.cs">
        The stamper already mints ids for id-less paragraphs; extend it to WRITE the minted `w14:paraId` into the retained package DOM and keep existing ids untouched (idempotent).
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration (🔒 RIGOR LEVEL: FULL + reason + protocol steps). Load knowledge files + `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. State the Placement Justification (extends `ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper` in `Services/Compose/`; reuses the extraction seam; no new surface). Run `/conflict-check` before touching `Services/Compose/`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Trace the current stamp path">Read `ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper`, `ParaIdPreParser`, and `AnnotationReanchorService.ExtractParaIds`. Confirm where the minted id is (or is not) written back into the package bytes today vs only carried in the projection map.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Persist minted ids into retained bytes">Extend the stamper to, for each editable `w:p` lacking a `w14:paraId`, mint a unique id and write it into the DOM (`w14:paraId` attribute, `w14` namespace) of the retained package, then save so the id lives in the retained bytes. Leave paragraphs that already carry an id untouched.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Cover table cells / nested tables">Reuse `ExtractParaIds`' document-order walk so table-cell and nested-table paragraphs are included; verify uniqueness of the id set across the whole document.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Idempotency + round-trip check">Verify a doc with pre-existing paraIds is not re-minted; verify a mint → save → reload preserves the ids. Keep the projection paraId map consistent with the persisted ids.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Build + facade + size/CVE">Build BFF; run existing `Services/Compose` unit tests; run the Tier-1 NetArchTest facade check. Publish; report size absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB; `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Close out">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If Word-regenerated paraIds collide (Word remints ids on external tracked-change saves) so that persisting on ingest cannot guarantee stable ids across cross-Word-session saves, STOP and note the boundary: this task owns same-session durable minting; the cross-session regen case is `AnnotationReanchorService`'s fuzzy fallback (I-7 last resort), not a fix in this task. Surface the boundary rather than expanding scope into re-anchoring.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper.cs (mints + persists `w14:paraId` into the retained package on ingest; idempotent)</output>
    <output type="report">Publish-size absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB; CVE scan; Placement Justification; NetArch facade result</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Every editable paragraph in the corpus docs resolves to a unique `w14:paraId` that is PRESENT IN THE RETAINED PACKAGE BYTES (not only in the projection map), including paragraphs inside table cells and nested tables.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Ids survive a load → save → reload round-trip (the same paragraph resolves to the same paraId after reload).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a document that already carries `w14:paraId` values on its paragraphs is NOT re-minted — existing ids are left byte-identical (idempotent).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Ids are written via OpenXml DOM mutation, never by string-editing `document.xml`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Services/Compose/` injects no AI-internal type (Tier-1 NetArchTest green); no `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/` (ADR-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF builds green; publish size reported absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline, ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Extends a KEEP-list asset — no `&lt;justification&gt;` block (modify-only, not new surface). The through-the-wire
    proof that persisted ids survive ingest lives in task 013's seam slice. Coordinate the `Services/Compose/`
    cutover with `spaarkeai-compose-r3` (deployed base).
  </notes>

